{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-277827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $6-\\sqrt[3]{10+3x}<2.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}6-\\sqrt[3]{10+3x} & <2 \\\\ -\\sqrt[3]{10+3x} & <-4 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{10+3x} & >4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the sign of the inequality since we divided by a negative number.\n\nThen, we cube both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{10+3x})}^{3} & >{4}^{3} \\\\ 10+3x & >64 \\\\ 3x & >54 \\\\ x & >18.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277827" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b42339288b320302545090fab399ed4f5d3556ce3e95bc1508c6271b13a469f2"} {"question" "q-277827" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277827" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math ">"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277827" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277827" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "18"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-115031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $\\sqrt[3]{2x+1}-1\\le 2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-115031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{2x+1}-1 & \\le 2 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{2x+1} & \\le 3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cube both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{2x+1})}^{3} & \\le {3}^{3} \\\\ 2x+1 & \\le 27 \\\\ 2x & \\le 26 \\\\ x & \\le 13.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-115031" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b42339288b320302545090fab399ed4f5d3556ce3e95bc1508c6271b13a469f2"} {"question" "q-115031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-115031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge -10"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{1}{5}"] ["math" "x\\le -\\frac{1}{2}"] ["math" "x\\le 13"] ["math" "x\\le 3"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-115031" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\le 13"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $2+\\sqrt[3]{7x+6}<0.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2+\\sqrt[3]{7x+6} & <0 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{7x+6} & <-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cube both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{7x+6})}^{3} & <(-2)^{3} \\\\ 7x+6 & <-8 \\\\ 7x & <-14 \\\\ x & <-2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277798" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b42339288b320302545090fab399ed4f5d3556ce3e95bc1508c6271b13a469f2"} {"question" "q-277798" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277798" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "<"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277798" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277798" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt[3]{6x-2}+8<10.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt[3]{6x-2}+8 & <10 \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}\\sqrt[3]{6x-2} & <2 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{6x-2} & <4.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cube both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{6x-2})}^{3} & <{4}^{3} \\\\ 6x-2 & <64 \\\\ 6x & <66 \\\\ x & <11.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277833" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b42339288b320302545090fab399ed4f5d3556ce3e95bc1508c6271b13a469f2"} {"question" "q-277833" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277833" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "<"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277833" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277833" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "11"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-87626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $\\sqrt[3]{4-3x}-2\\le 0.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-87626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Isolating the cubic term, we find\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt[3]{4-3x}-2 & \\le 0 \\\\ \\sqrt[3]{4-3x} & \\le 2.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we cube both sides and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(\\sqrt[3]{4-3x})}^{3} & \\le {2}^{3} \\\\ 4-3x & \\le 8 \\\\ -3x & \\le 4 \\\\ x & \\ge -\\frac{4}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that, in the last step, we had to flip the sign of the inequality because we divided by a negative number.\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -\\frac{4}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-87626" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b42339288b320302545090fab399ed4f5d3556ce3e95bc1508c6271b13a469f2"} {"question" "q-87626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-87626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["math" "x\\ge -\\frac{4}{3}"] ["math" "x\\ge 2"] ["math" "x\\ge \\frac{2}{3}"] ["math" "x\\le -4"] ["math" "x\\le \\frac{3}{4}"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-87626" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "x\\ge -\\frac{4}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-278213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $2\\sqrt{3x+6}+11\\ge 5.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-278213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\sqrt{3x+6}+11 & \\ge 5 \\\\ 2\\sqrt{3x+6} & \\ge -6 \\\\ \\sqrt{3x+6} & \\ge -3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the square root is greater than a negative number $(-3),$ so any number we can substitute into the square root will satisfy the inequality. So, the solution is the domain of the square root.\n\nTo find the domain, we recall that the expression under the square root must be greater than or equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n3x+6\\ge 0\\,⇒\\,x\\ge -2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge -2.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-278213" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b42339288b320302545090fab399ed4f5d3556ce3e95bc1508c6271b13a469f2"} {"question" "q-278213" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-278213" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-278213" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-278213" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "-2"] "category" "model_interpretation" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $2-\\sqrt{6x-2}<10.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2-\\sqrt{6x-2} & <10 \\\\ -\\sqrt{6x-2} & <8 \\\\ \\sqrt{6x-2} & >-8\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the sign of the inequality since we divided by a negative number.\n\nHere, the square root is greater than a negative number $(-8),$ so any number we can substitute into the square root will satisfy the inequality. So, the solution is the domain of the square root.\n\nTo find the domain, we recall that the expression under the square root must be greater than or equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n6x-2\\ge 0\\,⇒\\,x\\ge \\frac{1}{3}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\ge \\frac{1}{3}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277834" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "b42339288b320302545090fab399ed4f5d3556ce3e95bc1508c6271b13a469f2"} {"question" "q-277834" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277834" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\ge"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277834" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277834" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{1}{3}"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Solve the inequality $\\sqrt{5-10x}+2>-7.$\n\n$x$\n{{field-1}}{{field-2}}" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we isolate the square root:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\sqrt{5-10x}+2 & >-7 \\\\ \\sqrt{5-10x} & >-9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHere, the square root is greater than a negative number $(-3),$ so any number we can substitute into the square root will satisfy the inequality. So, the solution is the domain of the square root.\n\nTo find the domain, we recall that the expression under the square root must be greater than or equal to $0:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}5-10x & \\ge 0 \\\\ -10x & \\ge -5 \\\\ x & \\le \\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we had to flip the sign of the inequality since we divided by a negative number.\n\nTherefore, the solution is $x\\le \\frac{1}{2}.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13981580/state.json" "file_sha256" "654c86ef142201420cad09bff278f0f49779a39bf69c2afe7b10c27541fde326"} {"question" "q-277839" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course